## 3. Control Plane Node Upgrade Procedure

Perform all control plane upgrade steps directly on `kube-control-plane` (or `kube-cp-1`).

### Step 1: Update APT Repository to Target Minor Release (`v1.37`)

If crossing a minor version boundary (`v1.36` $\to$ `v1.37`), update the repository source and GPG key:

```bash
# Update GPG release key and repository source to target minor release v1.37
sudo curl -fsSL "https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/Release.key" \
  | sudo gpg --dearmor --yes -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc

echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc] https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/ /" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list

sudo apt-get update
```

Check the APT repository for the target release version string:

```bash
apt-cache madison kubeadm | head -n 5
```

Note the exact version string (e.g. `1.37.0-1.1`).

### Step 2: Drain the Control Plane Node (If Scheduling Workloads)

If non-system workloads are permitted to schedule on the control plane node, drain it first:

```bash
CP_NODE=$(kubectl get nodes --selector='node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane' -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}')

kubectl drain "${CP_NODE}" --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
```

### Step 3: Upgrade `kubeadm` Binary

Un-hold the `kubeadm` package, update repository metadata, install the target version, and re-hold the package:

```bash
TARGET_VERSION="1.37.0-1.1" # Target version from exam prompt

sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm

# Verify the updated kubeadm binary version
kubeadm version
```

### Step 4: Run Upgrade Plan

Execute `kubeadm upgrade plan` to validate cluster upgrade readiness:

```bash
sudo kubeadm upgrade plan
```

The output checks:

- Current control plane component versions (`kube-apiserver`, `kube-controller-manager`, `kube-scheduler`, `etcd`,
  `CoreDNS`).
- Target versions and API compatibility.
- Certificate expiration dates.

### Step 5: Apply the Control Plane Upgrade

Apply the upgrade using the target semantic version:

```bash
SEMVER="v1.37.0" # Target semantic version prefix 'v'

sudo kubeadm upgrade apply "${SEMVER}" --yes
```

`kubeadm upgrade apply` updates static pod manifests in `/etc/kubernetes/manifests/`, renews internal control plane
certificates, and updates cluster configuration ConfigMaps in `kube-system`.

### Step 6: Upgrade `kubelet` and `kubectl` on Control Plane

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
sudo apt-get install -y kubelet="${TARGET_VERSION}" kubectl="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

# Reload systemd daemon and restart kubelet
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
```

### Step 7: Uncordon the Control Plane Node

```bash
kubectl uncordon "${CP_NODE}"
kubectl get nodes
```

Verify that the control plane reports `v1.37.0` and status `Ready`.

