## 4. Secondary Control Plane Node Upgrade Procedure (HA Clusters: `kube-cp-2`, `kube-cp-3`)

In High-Availability clusters, secondary control plane nodes follow a distinct procedure from the primary control
plane. They must be upgraded **one node at a time** to maintain etcd quorum.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Secondary control planes must **never** run `kubeadm upgrade apply`. Only the first control plane executes `apply`.
> Secondary control planes execute `kubeadm upgrade node` to update their local static pod manifests from the cluster
> ConfigMap.

### Step 1: Drain Secondary Control Plane Node

From `kube-control-plane` (or `kube-cp-1`), evict workloads from the target secondary control plane:

```bash
CP2_NODE="kube-cp-2"

kubectl drain "${CP2_NODE}" --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
```

### Step 2: SSH into Secondary Control Plane & Update Repository

```bash
ssh "${CP2_NODE}"

# 1. Update APT repository source to v1.37 if crossing a minor version boundary
sudo curl -fsSL "https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/Release.key" \
  | sudo gpg --dearmor --yes -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc

echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc] https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/ /" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list

# 2. Unhold and install target kubeadm version
sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm
```

### Step 3: Upgrade Control Plane Configuration on Secondary Node

Execute `kubeadm upgrade node`:

```bash
sudo kubeadm upgrade node
```

This step fetches the cluster configuration from the `kubeadm-config` ConfigMap in `kube-system` and updates local
static pod manifests (`kube-apiserver`, `kube-controller-manager`, `kube-scheduler`, `etcd`) on this secondary node.

### Step 4: Upgrade `kubelet` and `kubectl` on Secondary Node

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
sudo apt-get install -y kubelet="${TARGET_VERSION}" kubectl="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

# Reload systemd daemon and restart kubelet
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

# Exit secondary control plane SSH session
exit
```

### Step 5: Uncordon Secondary Node & Verify etcd Quorum

From the primary control plane:

```bash
kubectl uncordon "${CP2_NODE}"
kubectl get nodes -o wide

# Verify all etcd endpoints report healthy before upgrading the next node
sudo ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  endpoint health
```

Repeat these steps sequentially for any remaining control plane nodes (e.g. `kube-cp-3`).

