## 5. Worker Node Upgrade Procedure

Unlike the primary control plane, worker nodes do not execute `kubeadm upgrade apply`. Instead, they execute `kubeadm
upgrade node` to update local kubelet configuration.

### Step 1: Drain the Worker Node (From Control Plane)

From the control plane node, safely evict workloads from the target worker node:

```bash
WORKER_NODE="kube-worker-1" # Replace with target worker node name

kubectl drain "${WORKER_NODE}" --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data --force
kubectl get nodes
```

The worker node status now reflects `Ready,SchedulingDisabled`.

### Step 2: SSH into Worker Node & Update Repository

```bash
ssh "${WORKER_NODE}"

# 1. Update APT repository source to v1.37
sudo curl -fsSL "https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/Release.key" \
  | sudo gpg --dearmor --yes -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc

echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.asc] https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/v1.37/deb/ /" \
  | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list

# 2. Unhold and install target kubeadm version
sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm
sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm
```

### Step 3: Upgrade Kubelet Configuration on Worker

Execute `kubeadm upgrade node`:

```bash
sudo kubeadm upgrade node
```

This step fetches the updated kubelet configuration from the cluster's `kubeadm-config` ConfigMap in `kube-system` and
writes it to `/var/lib/kubelet/config.yaml`.

### Step 4: Upgrade `kubelet` and `kubectl` Packages on Worker

```bash
sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl
sudo apt-get install -y kubelet="${TARGET_VERSION}" kubectl="${TARGET_VERSION}"
sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl

# Reload and restart kubelet daemon
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart kubelet

# Exit worker node SSH session back to control plane
exit
```

### Step 5: Uncordon Worker Node (From Control Plane)

From `kube-control-plane`, restore scheduling to the upgraded worker:

```bash
kubectl uncordon "${WORKER_NODE}"
```

### Step 6: Verify Cluster-Wide Node Readiness

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o wide
```

Confirm that all upgraded nodes display `Ready` status and report `v1.37.0`.

